  "summary": "Agentic systems are moving from data curation and analysis into drug discovery, biosynthesis red-teaming and physical laboratory execution.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is that agent utility depends on explicit grounding in provenance, memory and verifiable execution. El Agente Fármaco orchestrates scalable drug-screening workflows over a provenance-tracked molecule memory, benchmarked on 22 tasks, and PharmAgents2 describes an autonomous multi-agent system for end-to-end drug discovery with knowledge extraction and parallel agent scaling. Building Barricades red-teams agentic biosynthesis planning, motivated by the claim that LLMs and agentic software are eroding longstanding barriers to biotechnology. What is new relative to data-centric grounding is physical execution: AutoDNA, an AI-native experimental laboratory, reports more than 11,000 autonomous steps across over 20 instrument types for DNA synthesis, sequencing and storage. The set mixes one published item with three preprints, so evidence that grounded agents span computational and wet-lab execution remains early and largely descriptive.",
